{% comment %}
  Carbon Assist widget (all pages). Launcher uses true bottom-right; shifts left only when overlapping other fixed FABs.

  In Shopify Admin: Online Store → Themes → Edit code → Layout → theme.liquid
  Place these lines just before </body> (snippet `carbon-account-links-a11y` labels icon-only /account links):
    {% render 'carbon-account-links-a11y' %}
    {% render 'carbon-accessibility-widget' %}

  If your theme uses a different layout (e.g. theme.liquid only has sections), add the same renders
  to the main layout file that outputs </body>.

  Managed scope: loads the latest saved config from the Carbon app (Publish in /accessibility updates the DB;
  the storefront always fetches current settings). Do not use a static ?config= URL here or theme edits are
  required for every dashboard change.

  Bump `wrev` with `lib/carbon-a11y-widget-rev.ts` (CARBON_A11Y_WIDGET_WREV), then push this snippet.
{% endcomment %}
<script
  src="https://app.shopcarbon.com/accessibility/widget?scope=default&wrev=135"
  defer
></script>

<style>
  /*
    Mobile only: line the launcher up with the middle of the tawk.to chat
    bubble, which sits beside it in the bottom-right corner.

    The widget positions itself from JavaScript with an inline
    `inset: <top>px auto auto <left>px`, so this has to be !important to win,
    and it anchors to `bottom` rather than `top` because the mobile URL bar
    changes the viewport height and a fixed top value would drift with it.

    The maths: the chat bubble is 60px tall at bottom:20px, so its centre sits
    24 + 26 = 50px above the viewport bottom. This launcher is 52px tall, so
    bottom:24px puts its centre in the same place at any viewport height.

    `left` is deliberately left alone — only the vertical position changes, so
    the widget keeps the horizontal offset its own collision logic chose.
  */
  @media only screen and (max-width: 767px) {
    #carbon-a11y-widget {
      top: auto !important;
      bottom: 24px !important;
    }
  }
</style>
